# =============================================================================
# NivaSync Infotech — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (development) or `.env.production.local` (build) and fill
# in. Those files are git-ignored; this example file is the only one committed.
#
# ⚠ EVERYTHING PREFIXED `VITE_` IS PUBLIC.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* values into the JavaScript bundle at build time. Anyone can
# read them in the browser's source. Only values that are safe to publish belong
# here — a public endpoint URL is fine; an API key, SMTP password or CRM token is
# NOT. Those must live server-side, in a serverless function or in the form
# provider's own account.
# =============================================================================

# Public HTTPS endpoint that accepts a JSON POST from the inquiry forms.
#
# Leave unset and the forms use the documented mailto fallback: they state
# plainly that nothing was transmitted and offer a pre-filled email. They never
# show a false "message sent" confirmation.
#
# After setting this, you must also add the endpoint's origin to the CSP
# `connect-src` directive in `public/.htaccess`, or the browser will block the
# request. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
#
# VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://your-endpoint.example.com/inquiries
